<title>JAPAN: Panel proposes cut in Japan raw sugar tariff.</title>
<headline>Panel proposes cut in Japan raw sugar tariff.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>- A Japanese government advisory panel recommended on Wednesday that the country's import tariffs on raw sugar be lowered to 15 yen per kilogram from 20 yen per kilogram in the fiscal year beginning in April 1997.  </p>
<p>The Customs Tariff Council's recommendation was announced by the Ministry of Finance.  </p>
<p>&quot;Lower tariffs on raw sugar would improve our competitive edge against imported products,&quot; a senior official of the industry body said.</p>
<p>Japan imported 1,349,190 tonnes of raw sugar in the first 10 months of this year, against 1,411,071 tonnes in the same period last year, Finance Ministry data showed.</p>
</text>
